    "raw_solution": "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=0,\\pm 1$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at these points. Moreover, because $x=0,\\pm 1$ are simple roots, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at these points.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{II}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is positive, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $\\infty .$ Since only graph $\\text{IV}$ displays this end behavior, the correct answer is $\\text{IV}.$",
